  <data name="IndexRaceMethodNote.Text"><value>Monthly bars, adjusted. The source ignores the adjustment for an index, so every number already published on this board is unchanged — but a stock is another matter: a dividend is a cliff and a split is a halving, and neither is anything a holder lost. So an index row is a price return and a stock row a total return. Coverage differs: the S&amp;P reaches back to 1950, the Dow to 2009 and the Hang Seng Tech index to 2020. This board is not governed by the market setting: it reads three markets at once.</value></data>
